# Line endings are LF everywhere, decided here rather than by each clone.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Git for Windows ships 'core.autocrlf=true' in the GLOBAL
# config, and a submodule does NOT inherit the superproject's local config — it
# has its own '.git/config' and falls back to the global. So a checkout that had
# been carefully set to LF converted this repo to CRLF the moment
# 'git submodule update' touched a file, one file at a time as commits happened
# to change them. Observed 2026-09-01: the parent stayed LF while
# vendor/prinny-channel and vendor/pi-persona silently went CRLF, which broke a
# source-assertion test and re-stamped the sidecar runtime's source fingerprint.
#
# 'text=auto eol=lf' is checked into the repo, so it beats any client config and
# travels with a fresh clone on any platform. Nothing here is a Windows batch
# file, so nothing needs CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf
